  "_comment": [
    "Standard British-cryptic abbreviations: the one- to three-letter chunks a",
    "setter may drop into wordplay without signalling them further. Used by",
    "tools/clueability.py as legal charade / container pieces, so a word only",
    "counts as buildable if every piece is either a real word or listed here.",
    "",
    "This is a STARTER table and is meant to grow. When a clue-writing pass",
    "wants an abbreviation that isn't here, add it with its meanings rather than",
    "special-casing it — the same rule STYLE.md applies to feedback: encode it",
    "once, never rediscover it. Meanings are listed as the surface words a clue",
    "would use, so the later clue-writing stage can read them straight off.",
    "Keys are uppercase A-Z; values are lowercase clue words."
